{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790291811,"nonce":"U4QLZl4wi28pMJSMQa1VOAjsuH8=","title":"Switch guards never saw their bindings; nested nullary constructors bound as captures; closures in switch cases lost `this`","message":"Found while making haxe.macro.Printer run (Issue6531). All are pre-existing and affect ordinary code:\n\n1. `case C(x) if (x \u003e 0)` always fell through. MIR lowered the guard in its own block before binding the pattern's variables, so the guard failed to lower and was replaced by a jump to the next case.\n2. A no-argument constructor nested in a pattern (`case CString(s, SingleQuotes)`) was bound as a capture and matched anything. Printer printed every string single-quoted.\n3. `this` was captured by mutable reference. The lazy cell made at the first closure in one switch case was reused by a closure in a sibling case it does not dominate (\"Captured value not found in value_map\"), so Printer.printExpr did not compile.\n4. A method value inside a closure (`xs.map(function(x) return opt(x, show))`) lowered its `This` receiver to nothing. `This` was a leaf for capture collection, and a lambda maps its captured receiver under the named variable only. Arguments shifted.\n5. A recursive method with an inferred String return (printExpr \u003c-\u003e printExprs via `el.map(printExpr)`) typed the map result as Dynamic, and join read the raw strings as boxes.\n6. `eq(String, s)` with `s` an unannotated parameter: the generic call specialized on String while `s` stayed a Dynamic box, and the body read the box as a string. SIGSEGV.\n7. A Dynamic holding an Int, read as String (`var a:String = d`), was passed through as a string pointer. SIGSEGV.\n\nFix: bind before the guard; resolve a nested Var against the constructor parameter's enum (Null\u003cT\u003e unwrapped there only; unwrapping it for the top-level subject LOST Issue3061); capture `this` by value, and `This` as the receiver slot; pre-register a syntactically-String return as String; an unannotated Dynamic parameter bound to a String type variable is cast to String (a broader rule over any Dynamic LOST 16 rows: decayed scalars were unboxed); haxe_unbox_if_tag gives a scalar box's string for a String target.\n\nConformance 658 -\u003e 659 (Issue6531), 0 LOST.","files":null}]}